### skill.md  [instructions]
- name: prospect
-   Identify, evaluate, prioritize, and engage prospects across sales, partnerships,
-   recruiting, outreach, and business development. Use when someone needs to find the
-   right people or organizations to pursue before they become leads, clients, candidates,
-   or active opportunities.
- A prospect is not just a name on a list.
- A prospect is a possible fit that has not yet earned focused effort.
- Most prospecting fails because people confuse volume with opportunity. They gather contacts,
- build lists, and send messages, but never define what makes someone worth pursuing,
- what signals indicate fit, or what conditions would make outreach timely and relevant.
- This skill helps turn vague target-hunting into structured prospecting.
- ## Trigger Conditions
- Use this skill when the user needs to:
- - define an ideal prospect profile
- - find or prioritize potential clients, customers, partners, or accounts
- - build a prospecting workflow
- - qualify who is worth outreach
- - organize a target list before lead generation
- - improve outbound targeting
- - identify signs of fit, timing, urgency, or strategic relevance
- - reduce wasted effort on low-value outreach
- Also trigger when the user says things like:
- - "Help me find prospects"
- - "Who should I target"
- - "How do I build a prospect list"
- - "Which accounts are worth pursuing"
- - "What makes a good prospect"
- - "How do I prioritize outreach"
- - "I need better targeting"
- ## Core Principle
- Prospecting is not about finding the most names.
- It is about finding the right names, at the right time, for the right reason.
- A good prospect is not merely someone who could buy.
- A good prospect is someone whose needs, timing, constraints, incentives, and context
- make pursuit potentially worthwhile.
- This skill helps:
- - define prospect criteria before list-building
- - separate raw targets from real opportunities
- - prioritize prospects by fit, timing, and relevance
- - structure prospecting workflows and qualification logic
- - identify useful signals before outreach
- - reduce wasted effort and false positives
- - turn unstructured target-hunting into a repeatable system
- ## Default Outputs
- Depending on the request, produce one or more of the following:
- 1. Ideal Prospect Profile
- A structured definition of who should be targeted and why.
- 2. Prospect Scoring Framework
- A model for ranking prospects by fit, urgency, value, and accessibility.
- 3. Target List Strategy
- A plan for building and segmenting prospect lists.
- 4. Prospect Qualification Logic
- Rules for deciding who should be pursued, watched, or ignored.
- 5. Outreach Prioritization Plan
- A system for deciding where effort should go first.
- 6. Prospecting Workflow
- A repeatable process from identification to qualification to handoff.
- ## Response Rules
- When responding:
- - define what kind of prospect is being sought
- - identify the desired downstream outcome
- - distinguish total addressable names from viable prospects
- - make qualification criteria explicit
- - keep the system usable, not theoretical
